d": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2025-12-22T18:39:04Z", "updated_at": "2025-12-22T18:39:04Z", "body": "> What's the difference between telemetry.unix_epoch_time() and telemetry.subscribe_unix_epoch_time() ?\n\n- [subscribe_unix_epoch_time](https://mavsdk.mavlink.io/main/en/cpp/api_reference/classmavsdk_1_1_telemetry.html#classmavsdk_1_1_telemetry_1a172eb7793c61744a8195e38c0612ec1f) gives you a subscription, so your callback will be called each time a message with that information arrives in MAVSDK. This is an async API.\n- [unix_epoch_time](https://mavsdk.mavlink.io/main/en/cpp/api_reference/classmavsdk_1_1_telemetry.html#classmavsdk_1_1_telemetry_1ab5ea5f6bb35b5670e34d5697d8c880f4) just gives you the latest value at the time when you query it. This is a polling based API that you call every time you want to know the value.\n\n> Should I use set_rate_unix_epoch_time when I subscribe ?\n\nIt depends whether you want or require a certain rate. If your autopilot already sends it at an acceptable rate, you don't have to. If it doesn't send it at all, then yes, you have to request it.\n\n> Should I use a mutex inside of subscribe callback?\n\nIf you are writing or reading shared data from different threads (which the subscription callback is), then likely, yes, you want to add a mutex around the data, or use a `std::atomic` if it's just one value you set.", "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/3683535243/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/3684612274", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2741#issuecomment-3684612274", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2741", "id": 3684612274, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s7bnriy", "user": {"login": "AlexisAlexisM", "id": 222949038, "node_id": "U_kgDODUnurg", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/222949038?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexisAlexisM", "html_url": "https://github.com/AlexisAlexisM", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexisAlexisM/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexisAlexisM/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexisAlexisM/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexisAlexisM/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexisAlexisM/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexisAlexisM/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexisAlexisM/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexisAlexisM/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/AlexisAlexisM/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2025-12-23T00:14:16Z", "updated_at": "2025-12-23T00:14:16Z", "body": "Thank you for your answers.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactio